        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "404d8c40-44ea-5a3e-8b64-6fa7f20b1fc5",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Species: Phyllogomphus selysi\n- Taxonomy: Gomphidae\n- Places: Angola, Botswana, Cameroon, Republic of the Congo, Democratic Republic of the Congo, Kenya, Malawi, Mozambique, Namibia, South Africa, Tanzania, Uganda, Zambia, Zimbabwe, Burundi, Luanda, Atlantic Ocean\n- Topics: Country geography\n\nFacts:\n- Phyllogomphus selysi is a species of dragonfly in the family Gomphidae.\n- Phyllogomphus selysi is found in Angola, Botswana, Cameroon, the Republic of the Congo, the Democratic Republic of the Congo, Kenya, Malawi, Mozambique, Namibia, South Africa, Tanzania, Uganda, Zambia, and Zimbabwe, and it is possibly found in Burundi.\n- Angola is the seventh-largest country in Africa.\n- Angola is bordered by Namibia to the south, the Democratic Republic of the Congo to the north, Zambia to the east, and the Atlantic Ocean to the west.\n- Luanda is the capital and largest city of Angola.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
